WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.100
I've been waiting for that unwavering 
and endlessly shining sun!

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.650
I've been waiting for those clouds 
drifting through blue skies!

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.320
I've been waiting for the freedom 
to sleep in as late as I want!

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.990
It's here.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.740
It's here.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.240
It's here.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:20.740
It's here.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.500
It's finally here!

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.220
Summer vacation!

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.510
Hey!

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.510
It's so hot.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.730
Let's play!

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:12.730
Impossible.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.150
What?

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:19.210
I've got a bunch of people 
I must save.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.870
People to save?

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.740
What? Yukki, are you 
doing volunteer work?

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.740
I guess.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.250
After all, I'm motivated 
by more than just money.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.430
What's this? An incident?

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:36.200
Yuki, if you don't hurry it up, 
they'll all die.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.510
We can't be having that.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.980
What did Chizuru want?

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.270
Who knows?

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.270
Go home.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.900
I haven't even said anything yet!

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.920
I already know what you want.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.400
That makes things easy!

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.330
What do you want to do? Where should we go?

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.740
Hey, where should we go?

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.600
I'm said I'm not interested in going out!

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.410
I'm doing work!

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:04.910
See you later.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.420
Wait.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.520
Just one minute. Just talk 
to me for one minute.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.370
You have a minute to talk, don't you, Ma'am?

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.290
This'll make 
your skin silky-smooth, missus.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.300
What are you, a door-to-door salesman?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.920
Coming.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.050
Oh, Chizuru-kun.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.100
I'm surprised you found your way here.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.370
Are you free? Do you want to go out?

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.830
Huh? Um, well...

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.910
You can't either?

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.010
Oh, that's not what I meant.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.270
Let's see...

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.520
Would you like to join me?

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.690
Join you?

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.450
This is...

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.720
I was making snacks.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.990
I've never done it before,

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.980
but as we're on vacation, 
I thought I'd give it a go.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.710
Would you like to help me?

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.710
Why not?

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.040
Let's do it.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.310
Oh, good. Can you mix that dough for me?

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.220
This?

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.090
Yes.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.270
Chizuru-kun, you're good at that.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.320
Huh?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:12.060
There you go again. I'm still learning.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.240
That smells good.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:19.030
It really does. I hope it turns out well.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.630
Tastes about right.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:24.630
Shun-chan, that's no fair.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.510
Oh, sorry.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.380
Here.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:33.850
The delicious sweetness 
expands in my mouth.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:37.090
I look forward to seeing 
how they turn out.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.760
Me too.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.630
Once we're finished, we 
should take them to...

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.020
What is this strange feeling? 
It's like I'm losing myself.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:51.930
Um...

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.780
Are you bored?

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.020
Now that we've come this far, 
we should finish making...

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.430
Making what? A new me?

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:02.530
What?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.270
You wanted someone to hang out with,

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.630
so you went to everyone's houses.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.600
That's right. It's summer vacation,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.260
but everyone's hiding in 
the cool air of their rooms.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.390
It's especially hot today.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.360
But there's a whole month ahead of us,

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.630
so I'm sure there will 
be opportunities to...

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.050
What about a festival?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.300
A festival?

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.110
There's one today.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:32.690
It'll be cool at night and I'm 
pretty sure everyone would go.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.140
What do you think?

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.240
Shun-chan, thank you.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.430
Thanks to you, I think I'll 
have a wonderful summer.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.400
Everyone should have their own Shun-chan.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.970
Now I can begin to enjoy my...

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.980
It's her.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:55.030
Hey.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:00.130
I can't believe they didn't 
have anything smaller.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.100
That looks heavy.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.930
Need help carrying it?

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.210
I'm fine. Leave me alone.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:12.930
You should learn to accept 
the kindness of others.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.710
She looks like a sheep.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:24.290
Here's the invitation to the festival.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:28.270
"Can everyone make it? Let me know."

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.910
Of course I'll go!

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:32.950
Hey, what about you?

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:35.810
Hey!

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:40.540
<i>Shun-chan invited me to a festival.</i>

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.600
That was how our summer began.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.930
A Japanese festival!

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.840
Why are you wearing a yukata?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:52.300
Isn't that what you 
wear to a festival?

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.400
Who doesn't buy a baby chick at a festival?

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.810
Don't buy one. Our apartment 
doesn't allow pets.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.470
There's so much to do.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:08.030
There's so much, I don't 
know where to start.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.660
I know, right? I can't decide either.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.730
I'm hungry.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.540
Let's get something to eat.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.160
"Something"?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.110
No! Not just something!

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.740
As students, we don't 
have a large budget.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:30.170
If we don't make our choice carefully, 
we'll regret it for sure.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:34.050
But there are so many choices, 
I don't know what to pick.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.040
Calm down!

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:38.680
In a situation like this, start 
with the classics! We'll go with...

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.680
Takoyaki!

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.800
Hey.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:48.250
Why don't we all buy something 
different and share?

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:49.790
I see.

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:51.350
Good idea, Yutan!

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.990
You party boy!

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:56.050
<i>Is the plan that praise-worthy?</i>

00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:59.950
This is delicious.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.480
What a great idea.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.110
Yes, but...

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:05.990
Yuki!

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.510
Pass it around already!

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.980
Don't worry. It'll get around to you...

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:11.960
...eventually.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.760
A fight breaks out every 
time we buy something.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.720
How long are you gonna hold on to that?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.000
Don't worry. I'll eat it so 
you don't get fat, Mary.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.440
Mary?

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:30.860
Oh, yeah. Her hair's kinda fluffy like a sheep.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.390
A sheep?

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.350
Masaki-chan's is?

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.550
That's not true!

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.490
Ow!

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:39.490
What was that for?

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.390
Masaki-chan, where are you going?

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:44.630
Oh, um...

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:50.380
How cute.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.350
They really are.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:55.420
I really wanted one when I was little,

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:57.390
but I could never get one.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.390
Goldfish are so quick.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.250
Here, Shun-chan.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.150
Thank you, Masaki-chan.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:07.650
All right!

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:09.390
Here you are.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:12.210
Good luck, miss.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:14.890
You going for it, Mary?

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:17.730
Now!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:19.930
Wait!

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.420
Miss, don't know what 
you're doing, do you?

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.670
It rips! That thing rips!

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.670
Here's your consolation prize.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.630
Hey, Mary.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.480
I thought I could do it.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.180
Hey, Mary.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:49.940
Don't be so down about it. You almost got one.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.830
Don't touch me!

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.960
And why do you keep calling me Mary?

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.660
Don't give me weird nicknames!

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.910
Stop it. Cut it out.

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.280
Just leave me alone!

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.500
That hurt. I just came to cheer you up.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.010
She's not cute at all.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.670
Is Masaki-chan okay?

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.830
I can't help her.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.630
Masaki-chan.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.010
Forget her.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:17.930
If you get close...

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.390
Leave him.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:23.890
Here.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.440
Shun-chan.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.440
Think of it as a consolation prize.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.280
I'll treasure it.

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:37.280
I'll treasure it!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.410
What was that about?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:46.040
She gets mad at me, but treats Shun like that.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.490
Well, sorry, I'm no good 
at cheering people up.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:53.670
She doesn't laugh with anyone 
except Shun, anyway, right?

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.420
Let's go.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.060
Is that right?

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:00.300
Sounds like she's in love with...

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:03.350
Huh?

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.500
What?

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.810
What?! She is?!

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:12.230
I didn't realize there was 
romance bubbling under the surface!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:16.550
It's above the surface 
and completely obvious.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:20.570
Really? So that's why she...

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.580
She's not cute at all.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:36.340
What's the matter? Are 
you boys rookies, too?

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.010
Sorry.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:44.410
It's okay. This paper's too thin 
to catch anything that's alive.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.540
I'm sure that's the point of a game like this.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.150
I feel like it shows no 
respect for their lives.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:52.870
Hush.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.270
Value is subjective.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:00.410
His business is making a 
game of their lives.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.260
Don't you agree?

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.880
What a generous man.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.990
I can't believe he gave 
us five layers of paper.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:24.110
I caught so many goldfish 
I had to return them.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:27.180
I'm sure you did something 
to make him do that.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:30.640
But why Shun-chan?

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:36.980
He's the least manly of all of us and 
he's more cute than cool.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.610
If we're just talking about 
his face, he's my type.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.570
But that's not what 
we're talking about.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.090
What are you mumbling about?

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:46.280
But...

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:53.340
Sometimes you don't know why 
you like or dislike someone.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.350
Shun-chan!

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:58.120
Masaki-chan!

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:00.970
Doesn't she look like 
a sheep in a flock?

00:12:58.690 --> 00:12:59.830
Shun-chan!

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.160
She does.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.260
We should help her.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.270
Kaname.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.590
Hisako, you're here too?

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:11.810
Yeah.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:12.960
Onee-chan.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.140
Onee...

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.150
Oh, Kaname-kun. So you're here too.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.130
Yeah.

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:23.030
Do you want some?

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:25.450
Onee-sama!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:29.030
I'm Kaname-kun's friend, Chizuru.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:32.040
Would you like to set off 
some fireworks later?

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.900
I promise it'll be a wonderful night.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:35.910
Fireworks?

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.460
When did you make that plan?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.240
We don't have any fireworks.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:46.760
If love always went according to 
plan, there would be no heartbreak.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.430
They should sell fireworks 
at the supermarket.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:54.000
I think there's one nearby, 
so I'll go check it out.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.480
Should we go, too?

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.720
Okay.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:58.700
But...

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:03.820
It's okay. We were just saying it'd 
be nice to get out of the heat.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.730
I see. Thank you.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.000
Where's Shun-chan?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.950
The three of them went 
shopping for fireworks.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.110
What?

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:16.680
<i>It's okay. Don't worry.</i>

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:20.420
<i>I have the keyholder Shun-chan gave me.</i>

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.750
It's missing!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.170
Masaki-chan.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:27.400
Do you want to come with us?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.180
Uh, no. I'm fine.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.920
Really? Okay.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:44.590
It should be around here somewhere.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:47.700
Sorry.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.910
Excuse me.

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.850
<i>It's okay. Don't worry.</i>

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.600
<i>I'll just start from over there again.</i>

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:01.170
What are you doing?

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:04.220
Don't go off by yourself, Mary.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.010
Oh, you dropped something.

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:10.630
Seriously?

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:11.900
Leave me alone.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.600
What are you acting so tough for?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.560
What am I gonna do with you?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.740
We'll help you look—

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.670
I didn't ask for your help!

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:22.110
Listen, an attitude isn't going 
to make your flat chest—

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.360
Let's go, Yukki! Forget her!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:33.240
If you're going to search by 
yourself, try not to look so upset.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:41.750
Right after I said not to...

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.090
Mary.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.090
What is that?

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.740
So, you want us to help look?

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:56.560
Fine, but...

00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:59.300
Why are you so beat up, Chizuru?

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.230
Ask her.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:04.610
It cost 700 yen.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:11.530
It's pretty crowded from 
here to the shrine.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.150
It won't be easy.

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.370
Let's split up and search.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:20.490
Sensei! The class is trying to work together

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:24.090
but Yuta-kun isn't participating seriously.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:28.060
Yuta-kun, I know you 
want to look at girls,

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:29.510
but you've still got to try hard.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:30.610
You, too.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.210
Sensei, I found it.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.300
Found what?

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.960
Seriously?

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:43.690
Hey, shorty. Is that really it?

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:47.780
What is it, little girl?

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:49.490
That's it.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:54.780
I dropped that bear. Could I have it back?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:00.160
This? I found this thing.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.870
And she's the one who dropped it.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.010
Do you have any proof?

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:04.940
What?

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.820
If you don't have any 
proof, you can't have it.

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.130
But...

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.170
If you want it, shoot it down.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.550
300 yen per round.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:19.150
I promise to never grow up to be like him.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:22.540
I wouldn't say he's "grown up".

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:26.100
I can't believe he'd make 
something he found a prize.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.930
Thank you—

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.050
You idiot!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.790
I can't believe you let 
your emotions get to you!

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:38.740
Let go!

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:40.290
Calm down.

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:41.520
That's right.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:44.480
If you get emotional, you 
won't be able to aim properly.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.420
You're too calm about this!

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.520
Fine.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.500
I'll do it.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:54.800
All right.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:03.540
Hey, you shouldn't laugh at people 
who are trying their hardest.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:06.870
That was Kaname's best effort.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.690
You're not helping.

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:11.320
You can do it, Yutan!

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:16.320
With such a small target, 
this might be hard.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.760
That's right! It's not easy! Right?

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:20.910
For something like this...

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:25.870
we should rely on someone who's 
cleared countless missions before.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:28.510
Well?

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.090
The size of the target doesn't matter.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.950
Kill or be killed. That's 
all that matters.

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:36.970
It's not <i>that</i> serious.

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:44.310
What are you aiming at?

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.390
I couldn't choose between them.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.400
I don't believe you, Yuki.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.080
And now we're out of bullets.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.160
There's nothing we can do.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:00.780
They got the fireworks 
so they're coming back.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.620
<i>Shun-chan's coming back.</i>

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.120
<i>He'll know I dropped it.</i>

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.630
Sir, I need some bullets.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:12.630
What?

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.660
You're already paying with bills?

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:17.930
So much for saving money by sharing food.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:21.140
If I get it, you're 
paying me back, Mary.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.640
Whoops.

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:28.120
You're one to talk.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.140
Shut up.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:33.440
1 round (5 shots)
300yen

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:41.080
Damn it.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.780
What's wrong? You've got one shot left.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:45.990
I know!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.330
Should I take over?

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.330
You sit still.

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:50.080
Damn it.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:54.400
Who said I could do it 
if I fired enough shots?

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.780
Now I'm just wasting money.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:05.550
Namu... Namu... Namu... Namu...

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:10.020
Here.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:11.620
Thanks.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:16.550
What's a young girl like you 
chanting "namu namu" for?

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:21.220
But maybe that's why I managed to hit it.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.200
Who knows, huh?

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.390
You're right.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:37.380
They're back.

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:39.500
We're back.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:40.670
Welcome back.

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:42.700
We bought fireworks.

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:45.270
<i>I'm the one who got it back.</i>

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:45.370
Amazing. There's so many.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.180
We've got more.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:51.680
She's not cute at all.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.260
Let's fire them off together later.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.290
Yeah.

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:57.150
Should we save the sparklers for last?

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.690
Get too close to me,

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:05.560
and you'll get burned!

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:07.570
You're the one coming towards me!

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.820
Chizuru-kun, that's dangerous!

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:14.330
As the fireworks gently nudged back the night,

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.840
everyone's smiles were there as always.

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:23.130
A firework's glow is short lived,

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.430
just like your life.

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:29.810
If you don't stop playing 
around, you'll get hurt!

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:32.670
I can't believe they'd 
mess around like that.

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:35.530
Wielding fireworks is a serious contest.

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.650
No, they're not!

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:42.090
These obvious everydays are my treasure.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:46.070
If I keep them tightly held in my fist forever...

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:49.070
I know from time to time I'll softly 
open my hand and peer inside.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:51.090
I never thought that time would come.

00:21:52.690 --> 00:21:54.290
Look over here.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.260
<i>A photo with just me and Shun.</i>

00:21:56.260 --> 00:21:57.920
Here we go.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.600
That looks fun.

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:10.300
Go right ahead.

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:12.900
Don't hold back. Go enjoy yourself.

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:14.570
What?

00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:18.020
That's not what I meant.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:35.900
I probably won't realize it until I'm an adult.

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:44.880
"One Summer"

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:20.860
Next time: Glasses and Et Cetera
